header: T4 Knowledge Base
gives: Syllabus Head V taught from zero in simple English — the heaviest topic in the paper, asked in every year; Colonial and capitalist perspectives of gender, and the thesis that development is the new name of coloniality; A gender analysis of modernisation, dependency, world-system and structural-functionalist theory; WID, WAD and GAD; Moser's needs and roles, Kabeer's empowerment, gender mainstreaming; The gender critique of structural adjustment; globalisation and "gendered globalisation"; climate change; the MDGs and SDGs; Evidence and Pakistani examples inside every point, diagrams, today's debates, the record and five likely questions; About 125 MCQ-style one-liners, every past MCQ on the topic, and a detailed revision sheet
